==============================================================================
Part B: candidate closed form for T_prof, derived symbolically, then
        checked against Part A's Richardson-extrapolated numerics
==============================================================================
Full series (in x=1/m) of ln(term_m), to O(x^0) [constant term only,
all log(x)/log(m)-divergent pieces should have cancelled]:
  lambda**2/2 - log(gamma) - lambda**2/gamma

ser_const + log(gamma) [should be exactly -A*lambda^2 for some A(gamma)]:
  lambda**2*(gamma - 2)/(2*gamma)
=> -A(gamma) = (ser_const + log(gamma)) / lambda^2 = (gamma - 2)/(2*gamma)

>>> CANDIDATE CLOSED FORM: T_prof(lambda,gamma) = (1/gamma) * exp(-A(gamma)*lambda^2)
>>> A(gamma) = (2 - gamma)/(2*gamma)
>>> A(gamma) simplified = (2 - gamma)/(2*gamma)

